5. AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store

AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store provides centralized storage for configuration values and parameters.

It supports ordinary configuration values and encrypted SecureString parameters.

Key Features

* Store application configuration.
* Store encrypted parameters using AWS KMS.
* Organize parameters using hierarchical paths.
* Control access using IAM.
* Retrieve parameters programmatically.
* Integrate with EC2, Lambda, and deployment workflows.

Example

An application can store its configuration under paths such as:

* /production/app/port
* /production/app/database-host
* /production/app/database-password

Sensitive values should be stored as encrypted parameters with appropriate permissions.

Parameter Store vs Secrets Manager

Feature	Parameter Store	Secrets Manager
Main purpose	Configuration and parameters	Secrets and credentials
Encrypted values	Supported with SecureString	Supported
Automatic secret rotation	Requires a custom workflow where needed	Built-in rotation capabilities for supported configurations
Typical use	Configuration settings and feature flags	Database passwords and API credentials

Use Parameter Store for centralized configuration and appropriate encrypted parameters. Use Secrets Manager when managed secret lifecycle and rotation capabilities are important.

