11. AWS Shield

AWS Shield is a managed Distributed Denial of Service (DDoS) protection service.

DDoS attacks attempt to overwhelm an application or its network resources with excessive traffic.

AWS Shield Levels

AWS Shield Standard

* Provides automatic protection against common network and transport-layer DDoS attacks.
* Included automatically for AWS customers.

AWS Shield Advanced

* Provides enhanced DDoS protection for eligible supported resources.
* Offers additional detection, visibility, and response capabilities.
* Includes access to additional DDoS response support and other protections under its service terms.

Example

A public website receives a large volume of malicious traffic intended to make it unavailable. Shield helps protect supported AWS resources against qualifying DDoS attacks.

DevOps Use Case

Use Shield protection for internet-facing applications, particularly where availability is critical.

Shield vs WAF

AWS Shield	AWS WAF
Focuses on DDoS protection	Focuses on filtering web requests
Helps protect availability	Helps mitigate web-layer attacks
Includes automatic Standard protection	Uses configured rules and managed rule groups

They can complement each other.

