12. Amazon Macie

Amazon Macie is a data security service that helps discover and protect sensitive data stored in Amazon S3.

It uses machine learning and pattern matching to identify sensitive information.

Key Features

* Discover sensitive data in S3.
* Identify potential exposure risks.
* Detect certain types of sensitive information.
* Generate findings for investigation.
* Help assess S3 data security posture.

Example

An organization accidentally stores files containing sensitive personal information in an S3 bucket. Macie can help discover the data and identify potential security risks.

DevOps Use Case

Use Macie to discover sensitive data in S3 and investigate buckets that may contain information requiring stronger access controls.

Best Practices

* Review S3 bucket access policies.
* Enable appropriate encryption.
* Restrict public access.
* Investigate Macie findings and correct misconfigurations.

