17. AWS Certificate Manager (ACM)

AWS Certificate Manager helps provision, manage, and deploy supported SSL/TLS certificates.

These certificates enable encrypted communication between clients and supported endpoints.

Key Features

* Manage public and supported private certificates.
* Simplify certificate provisioning and renewal for supported certificates.
* Integrate with services such as Elastic Load Balancing and CloudFront.
* Support HTTPS for websites and applications.

Example

A web application uses an HTTPS listener on an Application Load Balancer. ACM can provide the certificate used to secure client connections to that listener.

DevOps Use Case

Use ACM to manage TLS certificates for supported public-facing applications and reduce manual certificate-management work.

Remember: ACM secures communication using certificates; it does not replace IAM or application authorization.

