18. AWS Firewall Manager

AWS Firewall Manager helps centrally configure and manage supported firewall and security protections across AWS accounts and resources.

It is especially useful in AWS Organizations environments.

Key Features

* Centrally manage supported AWS WAF policies.
* Manage supported Shield Advanced protections.
* Manage supported AWS Network Firewall policies.
* Apply security policies across accounts and resources.
* Help maintain consistent protection across an organization.

Example

A company operates several AWS accounts and wants a consistent WAF policy across its public-facing applications. Firewall Manager can help centrally manage supported policies.

DevOps Use Case

Use Firewall Manager in multi-account environments to standardize security controls and reduce configuration inconsistencies.

